valuation_customer: description, inputSchema  +discount_rate; lifetime_value needs revenue_per_period + retention_rate + discount_rate + margin; backlog needs contract_backlog + probability_of_completion + discount_rate; churn_impact needs current_customers + churn_rate_before + churn_rate_after + revenue_per_customer + -calls, rounded to 2 decimals; +calls; values carry the library's own precision (rates are decimals, so a royalty rate of 0.055 is not rounded);  parameters: +input.churn_rate_after input.churn_rate_after description: Churn rate after the change, as a decimal (0.10 = 10%). input.churn_rate_before input.churn_rate_before description: Churn rate before the change, as a decimal (0.10 = 10%). input.contract_backlog input.contract_backlog description: Backlog contracts as JSON objects with `value` and an optional `period` (default 1). input.current_customers input.current_customers description: Number of customers before the change. +input.margin input.margin description: Profit margin per period, as a decimal (0.20 = 20%). -discounted. +discounted.; li
valuation_discount_rate: description  -calls, rounded to 2 decimals; +calls; values carry the library's own precision (rates are decimals, so a royalty rate of 0.055 is not rounded);
