valuation_impairment: description, inputSchema  -standard). +standard); value_in_use needs cash_flow_projections + terminal_growth_rate + discount_rate; fair_value_less_costs needs fair_value (optional: disposal_costs, costs_to_sell); cgu_impairment needs cgu_carrying_value + cgu_recoverable_amount + goodwill_allocated + other_assets. +costs_to_sell. fair_value_less_costs takes exactly one of disposal_costs or -calls, rounded to 2 decimals; +calls; values carry the library's own precision (rates are decimals, so a royalty rate of 0.055 is not rounded);  parameters: +in currency units. input.cash_flow_projections input.cash_flow_projections description: Projected after-tax cash flows per period t=1..n, in currency units. input.cgu_carrying_value input.cgu_carrying_value description: Carrying value of the cash-generating unit, in currency units. input.cgu_recoverable_amount input.cgu_recoverable_amount description: Recoverable amount of the cash-generating unit, +input.discount_rate input.discount_rate description: Per-period discount rate as a decimal (0.10 = 10%). input.disposal_costs input.disposal_costs description: Costs of disposal, in currency units
valuation_income_methods: description, inputSchema  -and -charges. +charges, and the profit-split and analytical royalty methods. -contributory_asset_charges +cac_objects -contributory_asset_charges +cac_objects -assets. +assets; profit_split needs licensor_contribution_pct + licensee_contribution_pct + total_profit; analytical_method needs advantage_margin + volume + discount_rate + economic_life. -calls, rounded to 2 decimals; +calls; values carry the library's own precision (rates are decimals, so a royalty rate of 0.055 is not rounded);  parameters: +input.advantage_margin input.advantage_margin description: Margin attributable to the advantage over alternative technology, as a decimal (0.20 = 20%). -{value, +{type, value, +input.cac_objects input.cac_objects description: One object per period with total_cac, in currency units. mpeem also accepts a plain number, used as that period's charge. -input.contributory_asset_charges input.contributory_asset_charges description: Contributory asset charge per period t=1..n, in currency units. +input.economic_life input.economic_life description: Economic life in years (≥ 1). input.licensee_contribu
valuation_ip: description, inputSchema  -secrecy_probability. +secrecy_probability; patent_portfolio needs patents (optional: diversification_factor); option_pricing needs exercise_cost + expected_value + volatility + time_to_expiry + risk_free_rate. -calls, rounded to 2 decimals; +calls; values carry the library's own precision (rates are decimals, so a royalty rate of 0.055 is not rounded);  parameters: +input.diversification_factor input.diversification_factor description: Diversification adjustment applied as a decimal fraction of the portfolio sum, scaled by the portfolio's concentration (HHI): 0.10 is a 10% reduction only at full concentration. +input.exercise_cost input.exercise_cost description: Cost to exercise the option, in currency units. input.expected_value input.expected_value description: Expected value of the underlying asset, in currency units. -life. +life.; patent_portfolio = Total patent portfolio value with a diversification adjustment.; option_pricing = Patent valued as a
valuation_market_approach: description, inputSchema  -multiples or +multiples, -value. +value, score brand strength, and value a brand by Interbrand. +discount_rate; brand_strength_index needs revenue_stability + market_share + geographic_reach + customer_loyalty + investment_level; interbrand_brand needs brand_earnings + role_of_brand_index + brand_strength_score + -{revenue, multiple}; +{sale_price, revenue, asset_type}; +divides sale_price by revenue and -comparable +median implied -calls, rounded to 2 decimals; +calls; values carry the library's own precision (rates are decimals, so a royalty rate of 0.055 is not rounded);  parameters: -Optional multiplicative adjustments, e.g. {"size": 0.9, "growth": 1.1}. +Map from comparable index (0-based) to an adjustment applied as (1 + adjustment): {0: 0.10} raises the first comparable's multiple by 10%. input.brand_earnings input.brand_earnings description: Profit attributable to the brand, in currency units. input.brand_strength_score input.brand_strength_score description: Composite brand strength score on a 0-100 scale. -{revenue, multiple}. +{sale_price, revenue, asset_type}. input.customer_loyalty input.customer_loyalty description: Customer loyalty score from 0 to 1. +input.geo
valuation_royalty_analysis: description, inputSchema  -profit_attribution_to_ip). +profit_attribution_to_ip); brand_royalty_from_comparables needs comparable_rates (optional: brand_strength_adjustment). -calls, rounded to 2 decimals; +calls; values carry the library's own precision (rates are decimals, so a royalty rate of 0.055 is not rounded);  parameters: +input.brand_strength_adjustment input.brand_strength_adjustment description: Multiplied onto the comparable rate: 0.05 raises it by 5% of itself, not by 5 percentage points. +input.comparable_rates input.comparable_rates description: Comparable brand royalty rates as decimals (0.05 = 5%). -25%. +25%.; brand_royalty_from_comparables = Brand royalty rate derived from comparable licensing agreements. -"twenty_five_percent_rule"] +"twenty_five_percent_rule", "brand_royalty_from_comparables"]
valuation_simulation: description, inputSchema  ++ valuation_fn ++ valuation_fn -fixed_parameters. +fixed_parameters; monte_carlo_correlated needs valuation_fn + correlated_distributions + correlation_matrix (optional: iterations, seed); tornado needs function_name + base_params + parameter_ranges; scenario needs scenarios. -calls, rounded to 2 decimals; +calls; values carry the library's own precision (rates are decimals, so a royalty rate of 0.055 is not rounded);  parameters: +input.correlated_distributions input.correlated_distributions description: One object per sampled variable: `name`, `distribution` (normal, uniform or triangular) and `params`. Every parameter of the named `valuation_fn` must appear here, because the sampler supplies all of them. input.correlation_matrix input.correlation_matrix description: Correlation matrix as a JSON 2-D array of numbers, one row per variable, in the order of correlated_distributions. -all listed inputs, sum-based valuation.; +every input in input_distributions through the named valuation function.; -function. +function.; 
valuation_technology: description, inputSchema  +discount_rate; obsolescence_curve needs initial_value + obsolescence_rate + periods; algorithm needs computational_savings + deployment_scale + competitive_advantage_years + -calls, rounded to 2 decimals; +calls; values carry the library's own precision (rates are decimals, so a royalty rate of 0.055 is not rounded);  parameters: +input.competitive_advantage_years input.competitive_advantage_years description: Years the competitive advantage is expected to last. input.computational_savings input.computational_savings description: Annual computational cost saved, in currency units. input.deployment_scale input.deployment_scale description: Deployment scale multiplier applied to the algorithm's savings. +input.initial_value input.initial_value description: Value at the start of the period, in currency units. -discounted. +discounted.; obsolescence_curve = Technology value decay over time from obsolescence.; algorithm = M
valuation_time_value: description  -calls, rounded to 2 decimals; +calls; values carry the library's own precision (rates are decimals, so a royalty rate of 0.055 is not rounded);

